Validation of Measurement Procedures that Include Sampling — Eurachem (@cs-vampis: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_0H2SA2SC85XXDYT629N3E3KGXA
M. H. Ramsey, P. D. Rostron and F. C. Raposo, editors. Validation of Measurement Procedures that Include Sampling, Eurachem/EUROLAB/CITAC/Nordtest/AMC, first edition 2024. [Guide and citation](https://www.eurachem.org/index.php/publications/guides/vampis) · [Complete 68-file-page PDF](https://www.eurachem.org/images/stories/Guides/pdf/VaMPIS_2024_EN_v1.pdf).

Read the whole guide and reproduce both worked methodological studies. Extend the existing shared sampling and conformity knowledge into a supplier-to-receiver measurement process, including sample state, transport and analytical evidence. An excellent instrument result does not by itself validate the chosen lot sample.

Title, editors, contents and official release 17 December 2024 were checked on 29 October 2026. This supplements the separate method-validation and sampling-uncertainty guides. Free access and the guide's actual copyright/translation policy are distinct; unrestricted reproduction or translation is not inferred. No publication, dataset or figure is bundled.

